# CherDeal Operacional - AI Rules
These rules apply to any AI assistant working on this repository.

## 1. Project Architecture
The project consists of three services:
- `chdeal-frontend`: React + TypeScript frontend using Feature-Sliced Design (FSD).
- `chdeal-kanban-api`: Node.js Express API. This backend is migrating towards Clean Architecture.
- `chdeal-discord-bot`: Discord.js bot that receives webhook events from the API.

## 2. General AI Behaviors
- DO NOT use generic placeholder variable names.
- ALL comments in the code must be written in Portuguese (pt-BR) to accommodate the college team.
- Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` before making any significant structural changes.
- Always use `JSDoc` for backend functions and `TSDoc` for frontend hooks/components.
- Use GitHub markdown links when creating documentation artifacts.

## 3. Frontend Rules (chdeal-frontend)
- Strictly follow Feature-Sliced Design (app -> pages -> features -> entities -> shared).
- DO NOT import a feature from another feature.
- Use `Shadcn UI` components for building interfaces.
- DO NOT use Tailwind generic utility colors (e.g., `bg-red-500`). Stick to the curated theme variables defined in the project.
- Data fetching must be encapsulated inside `entities/*/api.ts` using TanStack Query. Components should NOT use raw `fetch` or `axios` directly.

## 4. Backend Rules (chdeal-kanban-api)
- DO NOT mix Business Rules, SQL queries, and HTTP routing in the same file.
- Follow Clean Architecture:
  - `domain/entities`: Business validation and pure JS objects.
  - `application/use-cases`: Orchestrates business logic.
  - `infrastructure/database`: All SQL queries (`pg-promise`) go here.
  - `interfaces/http/routes`: Express routes that only receive req/res and call the use case.
- Look at the `chdeal-kanban-api/_templates` folder for reference before coding.
- Keep the SSE (Server-Sent Events) patterns intact for real-time board updates.

## 5. Collaboration and Formatting
- Format code according to `.prettierrc`.
- Never commit actual secrets or `.env` files. Ensure they are in `.gitignore`.
